input/.git/HEAD makes input a git repository: outln applies .gitignore files only inside one.
== args
input
== file input/.git/HEAD
ref: refs/heads/main
== file input/.gitignore
*.gen.md
/build/
== file input/build/out.md
---
description: Build output (anchored /build/ ignores this).
---
# out
== file input/src/build/kept.md
---
description: Not the root build dir, so kept.
---
# kept
== file input/src/a.gen.md
---
description: Generated, ignored by root rule.
---
# gen
== file input/src/.gitignore
!keep.gen.md
local/
== file input/src/keep.gen.md
---
description: Re-included by nested negation.
---
# keep
== file input/src/local/l.md
---
description: Ignored by nested rule.
---
# l
== file input/other/local/o.md
---
description: Nested rule does not apply outside src.
---
# o
== stdout
glob view: input
Includes only a header or summary per file.
For file-level outlines, use `outln [FILE]...`.
input/other/local/o.md: description: "Nested rule does not apply outside src."
input/src/build/kept.md: description: "Not the root build dir, so kept."
input/src/keep.gen.md: description: "Re-included by nested negation."
